# What NOT to upload to EAS Build.
#
# EAS archives from the git root, so a mobile build was shipping the whole
# monorepo: 16.9MB, of which apps/web alone is 11MB. The Android build reads
# apps/mobile and the three packages it links to, and nothing else. A 16.9MB
# upload also fails more often than a 2MB one, which is what prompted this: a
# build died with ECONNRESET partway through the tarball.
#
# IMPORTANT: when this file exists, EAS uses it INSTEAD of .gitignore, not in
# addition to it. Everything .gitignore excludes has to be repeated here or it
# gets uploaded, and the first thing that would land in the tarball is every
# node_modules directory in the repo. Keep the two in step.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Repeated from .gitignore
# ---------------------------------------------------------------
logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
lerna-debug.log*

node_modules
dist
dist-ssr
.output
.vinxi
.tanstack/
.nitro
*.local

.vercel/

.env
.env.local
apps/api/.env
apps/api/.env.local

/docs/
/scratch_*
/artifacts/
*.tok
*.token

.vscode/*
.idea
.DS_Store
*.suo
*.ntvs*
*.njsproj
*.sln
*.sw?
/CLAUDE.md
.claude/
/LAUNCH.md

supabase/.temp/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Not needed by a mobile build
#
# packages/ is deliberately absent from this list. apps/mobile links to
# @everlumen/shared, @everlumen/db and @everlumen/api-client through `file:`
# paths, so excluding them would break npm install on the build worker.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------
apps/web/
apps/api/
supabase/
tests/
scripts/
.github/
